.TH READTHROUGH 1 "2026-09" "readthrough" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
readthrough \- multi-pass LLM code audit with resumable state and coverage accounting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readthrough
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a codebase through several independent lenses, merges what they find,
and accounts explicitly for what was and was not covered \(em so the result
is an audit with a known scope rather than an impression.
.PP
State is kept in a scan database, so an interrupted run resumes instead of
starting again, and reports can be rebuilt without re-reading anything.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI scan " PATH"
Scan one repository.
.TP
.BI multi " LIST"
Scan many: a file of paths, or a directory of repositories.
.TP
.BI report " DIR"
Rebuild reports from an existing
.IR scan.db .
.TP
.B lenses
List the available lenses.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Scope
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR" ", " \-\-out " DIR"
Output directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-ext " LIST"
Restrict to these extensions, e.g.
.BR py,ts .
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " GLOB"
Glob to exclude. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Only the N largest eligible files.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-loc " N"
Skip files smaller than this (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-file\-bytes " N"
Skip files larger than this (default 400000).
.SS Passes
.TP
.BI \-\-lenses " LIST"
Comma-separated lenses to run; see
.BR "readthrough lenses" .
.TP
.BI \-\-repeat " N"
Identical repeats per lens, to counter sampling variance (default 1).
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Second-opinion pass over the merged findings.
.TP
.BI \-\-verify\-min\-severity " LEVEL"
.BR critical ,
.BR high ,
.B medium
or
.B low
(default high).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Ignore cached results and redo every pass.
.SS Model and throughput
.TP
.BI \-\-model " MODEL"
Model to use.
.TP
.BI \-j " N" ", " \-\-workers " N"
Concurrent workers (default 6).
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk\-lines " N"
Lines per chunk (default 350).
.TP
.BI \-\-overlap " N"
Overlap between chunks, in lines (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-tokens " N"
Output token ceiling per request (default 8000).
.TP
.BI \-\-thinking " BUDGET"
Enable extended thinking with this token budget.
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " T"
Sampling temperature.
.SS Dry runs
.TP
.B \-\-fake
Offline stub: exercises the pipeline for free.
.TP
.B \-\-estimate\-only
Report what the run would cost, and stop.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Less output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan completed.
.TP
.B non-zero
The scan could not be run or resumed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Audit a repository:
.PP
.RS
.B readthrough scan . \-o audit/
.RE
.PP
Price it first:
.PP
.RS
.B readthrough scan . \-\-estimate\-only
.RE
.PP
Rebuild the reports later:
.PP
.RS
.B readthrough report audit/
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gradebook-code (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/readthrough
